# The state lives in its own git repository. It stopped being ephemeral - the
# interaction clock, the read cursors and the inbox are records of what you have
# done and none of them can be re-derived - so it is worth a history, but not
# this one: mixed in here it buried the diffs that matter in the diffs that do
# not, and dirtied the tree on every refresh. `WORKLOG_DATA` points elsewhere.
data/

# A clone of Term.jl, kept here because this directory is the only one that
# survives the sandbox. It is somewhere to fix the three `TermMarkdown` bugs
# this program works around - `Term.jl/fixme.md` is the write-up of them, and
# is excluded from that checkout too so it cannot end up in a pull request.
/Term.jl/
